# data
datasets/*
!datasets/.gitkeep
# The KU Leuven metadata is a committed source file, not a derived artifact: it is
# three keys of text recording the channel order and the provenance that the
# conversion depends on, and it carries no signal from the dataset. Git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded, so the directory is
# re-included only far enough to reach it; everything beside it (the .mat files,
# stimuli/ and the multi-gigabyte converted/ tree) stays ignored.
!datasets/AAD-KULeuven/
datasets/AAD-KULeuven/*
!datasets/AAD-KULeuven/metadata.json
models/*
!models/.gitkeep

# Everything derived from a dataset stays out of git, including the precomputed
# speech envelopes under datasets/audio/. The envelopes are the artifact the
# demo refuses to run without, but they are reproducible from the source audio
# plus the recorded SHA256 and parameters, so the repository keeps the recipe
# (scripts/auditory/envelopes.py) and not the megabytes.
datasets/audio/*
!datasets/audio/.gitkeep

# Demo output: rendered stereo mixes, replay products and per-run reports are
# derived artifacts, not sources. Committed results live under results/.
/output/auditory_demo/
/output/auditory_ui/

# editor
.vscode

# python
.venv
uv.lock
uv.toml
*.egg-info/
*.egg
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
dist/

# Local comparison material and disposable verification outputs.
/tmp/
/.tmp_tests/
.tmp_mne_home/
.tmp_uv_cache/

# recorded runs and generated outputs (keep the folders, not their content)
records/*
!records/.gitkeep
results/*
!results/.gitkeep
# Exception: the frozen pre-change test baseline is a reviewable text record of
# what the tree passed before the integration work started.
!results/test_baseline_*.txt
# Exception: the KU Leuven conversion summary is the reviewable evidence for
# step 2 (shape/rate/label invariants, naming derivation, on-disk size). The
# converted trials it describes stay out of git under datasets/.
!results/kuleuven_conversion_*.json
# Exception: the step-4 data audit is the reviewable evidence for the frozen
# feature contract (per-trial shapes, durations, labels, the group map, the
# channel subsets and the unit convention). It is derived from the dataset but
# contains no signal, only measurements, and step 5 is measured against it.
!results/kuleuven_audit.md
!results/kuleuven_audit_*.json
# Exception: step 5's decoder metrics are the reviewable evidence for the two
# contracts (the 64-channel baseline and the 20-channel live rig) and the two
# evaluation schemes, with per-class recalls beside the accuracy because the
# labels are 80/20 imbalanced. Derived from the dataset, but they carry
# measurements rather than signal, and the models they describe stay out of git
# under models/.
!results/aad_*.json
!results/aad_*.md
# Exception: the ANT test-set reference report. Every fact in it was measured from
# the user's own recording, and every value an outside reader needs (channels,
# units, markers, timeline, audio identity) is stated with the command that
# produced it, so it can be cited instead of re-derived. It is operator-confirmed
# where the files cannot settle a question, and says so. The recording it
# describes stays out of git under tmp/.
!results/antneuro_testset_report.md
# Exception: the live-blocking and offline-replay parity report. It is the only
# account of that check, it is small, and an ignored file is one `git clean -x`
# away from being lost.
!results/streaming_test_report.md
# Exception: step 8's session run records are the reviewable evidence that the
# replay path, the producer and the transport agree. Each record holds the trial,
# the explicit run policy, the session summary, the assertion verdicts and a
# bounded packet excerpt - measurements and packet payloads (decision words,
# correlations, gains, candidate file names), no signal and nothing that
# identifies a participant. The packet streams themselves and the rendered
# dashboard stay out of git under output/auditory_ui/.
!results/auditory_session_*.json
# Exception: the same step's frontend evidence is the dashboard rendered to
# static HTML by the vendored frontend's own components, fed with the packets a
# session published. It is the closest thing to the screenshot this repository's
# test path can produce, and it is 8 KB.
!results/auditory_frontend_*.html
# Exception: step 9's media run records. They are the evidence that the browser's
# own handshake was answered field by field, that the position in the attention
# and gain packets is the one the controller reported rather than one this process
# invented (decision D-02), and that the vendored frontend's gain gate actually
# opened. They contain the exchange log (action, reported position, acknowledged
# revision, round trip), the |dt| distribution and the gate's clause verdicts -
# measurements and protocol fields, no audio and no participant data. The rendered
# WAV, the packet streams and the gate output stay out of git under
# output/auditory_ui/. The mutation record is here for the same reason: it is this
# step's section 6.4 obligation and it is one JSON file.
!results/auditory_media_*.json
!results/media_mutations.json

# macOS metadata. On exFAT (this repository lives on one) macOS cannot store
# extended attributes, so it writes an AppleDouble sidecar next to every file it
# creates: "._relay.py" beside "relay.py". Those are metadata, not content, and
# they otherwise sweep into `git add -A` by the hundred.
._*
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
